{
  "verdict": "REQUIRED-FINDINGS",
  "requiredFindings": [
    {
      "id": "RF-J3A-1",
      "severity": "P2",
      "title": "Pin the private ReservedExecutionId::reserved constructor in X8",
      "location": {
        "path": "crates/host/tests/admission_tests.rs",
        "line": 813
      },
      "relatedLocations": [
        {
          "path": "crates/platform/src/lib.rs",
          "line": 125
        }
      ],
      "authority": {
        "path": "docs/implementation/m2/refusal-suite-x8/PROPOSAL-r3.md",
        "item": "3, row F and 3a",
        "line": 147
      },
      "finding": "The J3a case-table census says neither new identity type has a non-public inherent constructor, but ReservedExecutionId::reserved([u8; 16]) is a private inherent function returning Self. No J3a case calls it. X8 item 3a requires every non-public inherent function of the new row-D type to be listed and given a refusal case; the feature-only injected-reservation case covers a different function.",
      "impact": "The current private boundary works, but the required refusal coverage is incomplete. Making reserved public would allow construction without inserting into ExecutionIdReservations; none of the sixteen added cases would exercise that constructor. The passing driver census checks listed fixture files, not completeness of inherent-function coverage.",
      "evidence": "Against the driver-created plain opensip-platform metadata on rustc 1.95.0, reserve_execution_id() compiles, while ReservedExecutionId::reserved([0; 16]) returns exactly one coded diagnostic, E0624: associated function `reserved` is private.",
      "requestedChange": "Add the group-F fixture, its lawful control, exact E0624 annotation and J3a case-table row; correct the census text and include the new file in the inventory candidate, successor, subject and staged-lock pins. Alternatively remove the private inherent helper and construct the value directly only within the uniqueness-checked registry paths, so the stated census becomes true. Re-pin the product diff for the next review."
    }
  ],
