  "judgmentCalls": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "answer": "YES",
      "assessment": "Crate-private durable entry/results and the lending accessor fit J3a before J3d wires the host consumer. The public ingress admits no caller-provided home, profile, producer or release selector."
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "answer": "YES",
      "assessment": "The inject-id reservation belongs in the existing feature-only crash_barrier module. It checks the exact execution-id grammar and inserts into the same process registry before constructing the sealed value; a malformed id is Grammar/invariant and a duplicate is Reserved/host-I/O. The point name, placement and projected payload stay unchanged. This decision is acceptable; RF-J3A-1 concerns the separate private inherent helper on the plain surface."
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "answer": "YES",
      "assessment": "The probe is one walk charged to attempt A, using its platform premise and actor H/filesystem policy. Retained walk handles drop before the route, and admission independently walks under the fence."
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "answer": "YES",
      "assessment": "The after-token entry differs only at slot allocation and shares the ordinary producers/admit_receipt composition. The no-argument settlement-sweep entry and one gate are preserved."
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "answer": "YES",
      "assessment": "The two J-C2 halves join the lent identity to P0 and to host projection. J-C4b reserves three distinct prelude/session/render identities; the render draw site remains J3d. LostRace and NotPristine exercise actual scratch-chain ordinary admission through R12 and a reserved CommitSession. Those are adequate for J3a; an emitted envelope, real render pipeline and commit remain J3d obligations and are not discharged here."
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "answer": "YES",
      "assessment": "IDS_COST is byte-identical. Copying the lent RequestId and drawing/reserving the prelude ExecutionId occurs within the same charged step and before disclosure/P0 staging."
    },
    {
      "id": 7,
      "answer": "YES",
      "assessment": "The shared invocation RequestId cannot distinguish intents. The process-unique reserved ExecutionId binds parent preparation to exactly one intent without changing request correlation; the changed parent-test expectation follows that binding."
    },
    {
      "id": 8,
      "answer": "YES",
      "assessment": "The withdrawn creator-lent route is replaced by the required first-use/steady-state composition. The old refusal maps are byte-identical, and representative_refusals_choose_their_rows changes only formatting. Other fixture edits lend a drawn identity or project the reserved ExecutionId."
    }
  ],
  "leadRulings": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "answer": "AGREE",
      "assessment": "R10 is not wired here and TrustInvocation is byte-identical. Naming and reserving its operation identity, and the typed host handoff, remain a J1/J3d obligation; neither the prelude nor the later analysis-session identity is silently assigned to it."
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "answer": "AGREE",
      "assessment": "The understated inventory descriptions remain inherited under the explicit lead ruling. Carry them to the next description-only successor, without treating this inventory approval as that successor."
    }
  ],
  "sourceAssessment": [
    {
      "area": "identities",
      "result": "PASS with X8 coverage finding",
      "assessment": "RequestAuthority reserves drawn identities and lends only the identity behind its own pointer-identical reserved context; project stays unchanged. The single Mutex/BTreeSet execution registry redraws up to eight times, reserves before constructing the public value, and never removes a reservation. Prelude and CommitSession hold the reservation and expose only its projection. No literal/default/clone/serde/conversion construction is admitted on the plain surface."
    },
    {
      "area": "entry and two slots",
      "result": "PASS",
      "assessment": "Production enter_durable_analysis uses Native owners: fresh producers, charged presence probe, then exactly Present or PositivelyAbsent. Present seals attempt A with no intent/notice; absence runs the creator act by value and drops its producers before the returned non-Clone private token allocates B. No third allocation or second gate is admitted."
    },
    {
      "area": "creation record and refusals",
      "result": "PASS",
      "assessment": "Created holds only backup classification and disclosed PathBuf. Published and typed AfterRename yield Some, including the unchanged publication wrapper for a post-rename ledger refusal. LostRace/NotPristine and indeterminate/not-performed rename yield None. Every attempt-B failure carries the same record. All existing exhaustive refusal maps are byte-identical."
    },
    {
      "area": "tests",
      "result": "PASS with RF-J3A-1",
      "assessment": "Independent focused runs pass 4 platform, 6 host, 24 security and 1 complete X8-driver tests. Runtime controls cover J-C2, J-C4b and J-C5 through J-C9 with J-C6b at the declared J3a boundary. Listed J-C4/X8 cases work; the private reserved helper is omitted from the required constructor census."
    },
    {
      "area": "successors and existing behavior",
      "result": "PASS",
      "assessment": "S2/S3 replace the creator route with fresh ordinary admission. S4 records the lent RequestId and reserves the prelude id. S5-S7 leave store/trust/registration inside ordinary admission, and S10.1 reserves the session id at its existing draw point. Manifests, Cargo.lock, TrustInvocation, gate owner, crash-matrix site list, checker, and all matrix test/required-run files outside the changed-file list are unchanged. The commit outcome still projects the same id; the stopped session retains the reserved value."
    },
    {
      "area": "X9 lead sets",
